This is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it under
the same terms as the Perl 5 programming language system itself.

Full license text is available at:

<http://dev.perl.org/licenses/>

=end markdown


=head1 webdyne.pagi


=head1 NAME

webdyne.pagi - PAGI application runner for WebDyne


=head1 SYNOPSIS

C<<< webdyne.pagi [--option] <document_root> >>>

C<webdyne.pagi --port 8080 /var/www/html>

C<webdyne.pagi --test>


=head1 DESCRIPTION

C<webdyne.pagi> is a PAGI application script that handles web requests using the WebDyne framework. It builds a C<WebDyne::PAGI> application, loads any configured PAGI middleware, and starts it through C<PAGI::Server::Runner>.

The underlying C<WebDyne::PAGI> application can dispatch PAGI scope types for normal HTTP requests, server-sent events, WebSocket connections, and lifespan startup or shutdown events.


=head1 OPTIONS

C<webdyne.pagi> parses a small set of wrapper options itself and passes remaining command line options through to C<PAGI::Server::Runner>.

Wrapper defaults can be preloaded from C<~/.webdyne.pagi.opt> by creating an anonymous hash of option names and values.

Wrapper options handled by C<webdyne.pagi> itself:

=over

=item *

B<--test>

Use WebDyne's internal test page as the root.



=item *

B<--static>

Enable or disable PAGI static-file middleware.



=item *

B<--index>

Enable or disable directory index handling. With the default enabled setting, C<--index> uses WebDyne's built-in dynamic index page.



=item *

B<--index=FILE>

Use C<FILE> as the default document for directory requests instead of the built-in dynamic index page. Use the equals form so the document root argument is not consumed as the index value.



=item *

B<--root>

Set the document root. If omitted, the final non-option command line argument is used. If neither is supplied, C<DOCUMENT_ROOT> or the current working directory is used.



=item *

B<--env>

Set the PAGI environment mode to C<development>, C<production>, or C<none>. The wrapper sets C<PAGI_ENV> and forwards the mode to C<PAGI::Server::Runner>.



=item *

B<--argv>

Supply additional arguments that the wrapper prepends to the remaining command line arguments before invoking C<PAGI::Server::Runner>.



=item *

B<--dump_opt>

Dump the processed option hash and exit.



=back

Remaining command line options are handled by C<PAGI::Server::Runner>. Some common options are:

=over

=item *

B<--host>

Which host interface to bind to. When launched through C<webdyne.pagi>, the wrapper adds C<--host 0.0.0.0> unless a C<--host> option is present.



=item *

B<--port>

Which port to bind to.



=item *

B<--server>

Which PAGI server class to use. The runner default is C<PAGI::Server>.



=item *

B<--loop>

Event loop backend.



=item *

B<--lib>

Add a library path to C<@INC>.



=item *

B<-M>

Load a module before the app starts.



=item *

B<--default-middleware>

Enable or disable runner default middleware.



=item *

B<--daemonize>

Run as a background daemon.



=item *

B<--access-log>

Configure access logging.



=back

Additional runner process and output controls are passed through to
C<PAGI::Server::Runner>; see that runner's documentation for details.

On macOS, if no C<--port> option is passed through to C<PAGI::Server::Runner>, the wrapper uses port C<5001> to avoid conflicts with the default port. Other platforms use the normal runner default unless a port is supplied.


=head1 EXAMPLES

To run the script for basic functionality and serve files from C</var/www/html>, use:

C<webdyne.pagi /var/www/html>

Disable wrapper-managed index handling and rely on the PAGI request layer's default document behaviour instead:

C<webdyne.pagi --no-index /var/www/html>

Use C<home.psp> as the default document for directory requests:

C<webdyne.pagi --index=home.psp /var/www/html>

Start in production mode:

C<webdyne.pagi --env production /var/www/html>

Start on another port:

C<webdyne.pagi --port 8080 /var/www/html>

Start with a specific host:

C<webdyne.pagi --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080 /var/www/html>

Start with the internal test page:

C<webdyne.pagi --test>

Start with a different event loop backend:

C<webdyne.pagi --loop EV /home/aspeer/public_html>


=head1 ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

This script is a frontend to the WebDyne PAGI stack. It uses WebDyne configuration and environment handling.

=over

=item *

B<DOCUMENT_ROOT>

Supplies the document root when neither C<--root> nor a final non-option document root argument is provided.



=item *

B<DOCUMENT_DEFAULT>

Supplies the default C<index> value before C<~/.webdyne.pagi.opt> and command-line options are applied. This means explicit CLI index options override the environment, and C<~/.webdyne.pagi.opt> also overrides the environment. When the script is loaded by C<pagi-server> instead of run directly, the PAGI constant layer default is C<app.psp>.



=item *

B<PAGI_ENV>

Supplies the PAGI environment mode when C<--env> is not provided.



=item *

B<WEBDYNE_>*

Supplies the relevant WebDyne settings used by the PAGI modules.



=back

When the PAGI app is built, the wrapper also reads local WebDyne configuration from C<DOCUMENT_ROOT/.webdyne.conf.pl>. This applies both when C<webdyne.pagi> is launched directly and when it is loaded by an external PAGI server.

Relevant PAGI-specific settings from C<WebDyne::PAGI::Constant> include:

=over

=item *

B<WEBDYNE_PAGI_STATIC>

Enable or disable static-file serving middleware.



=item *

B<WEBDYNE_PAGI_MIDDLEWARE_STATIC>

Regular expression used to decide which static files are served directly.



=item *

B<WEBDYNE_PAGI_MIDDLEWARE>

Middleware stack applied around the WebDyne PAGI app.



=item *

B<WEBDYNE_PAGI_ENV_KEEP / WEBDYNE_PAGI_ENV_SET>

Environment variables preserved or injected for request handling.



=back


